projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE244nnn/GSE244645/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA1023957"},"200254613":{"uid":"200254613","accession":"GSE254613","gds":"","title":"Genome-wide analysis reveals the repression of MORC3 on PD-L1 expression in head and neck cancer","summary":"The expression and roles of MORC3 in cancers remain largely unknown. To understand the expression and roles of MORC3 in head and neck cancer, MORC3 was knocked down in CAL 27 cells with siRNA. Total RNAs were collected for mRNA sequencing assay.","gpl":"24676","gse":"254613","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2024/10/02","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM8047038","title":"NC_3"},{"accession":"GSM8047040","title":"N102_2"},{"accession":"GSM8047037","title":"NC_2"},{"accession":"GSM8047039","title":"N102_1"},{"accession":"GSM8047036","title":"NC_1"},{"accession":"GSM8047041","title":"N102_3"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":6,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["39329063"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE254nnn/GSE254613/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1071138"},"200277859":{"uid":"200277859","accession":"GSE277859","gds":"","title":"Targeting YAP/TAZ-TEAD as a precision therapy approach in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","summary":"Dysregulation of the Hippo pathway and the consequent activation of its downstream targets, the transcriptional co-activators YAP and TAZ (YAP/TAZ), drives oncogenic transcriptional programs upon binding TEAD transcription factors in multiple human malignancies. The recent development of small molecule TEAD inhibitors (smTEADi) provides an opportunity to therapeutically target Hippo pathway dysregulation in cancer. In this regard, HPV-negative head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) harbor multiple genetic alterations that promote YAP/TAZ hyperactivation, raising the possibility that HNSCC cells might be dependent on YAP/TAZ-TEAD driven oncogenic transcriptional programs. To test this hypothesis, we examined the antitumor activity of the novel smTEADi, SW-682 and genetically encoded TEAD inhibitor peptide (pTEADi) in Cal33 HPV-negative HNSCC cell line-derived xenograft model. To elucidate the transcriptomic changes upon YAP/TAZ-TEAD inhibition, RNA extracted from xenograft tumors treated with SW-682 or pTEADi, as well as control, was subjected to RNA sequencing.","gpl":"24676","gse":"277859","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2024/10/01","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM8532788","title":"Cal33 CDX Vehicle, rep2"},{"accession":"GSM8532791","title":"Cal33 CDX pTEADi, rep2"},{"accession":"GSM8532794","title":"Cal33 CDX Control, rep2"},{"accession":"GSM8532792","title":"Cal33 CDX pTEADi, rep3"},{"accession":"GSM8532795","title":"Cal33 CDX Control, rep3"},{"accession":"GSM8532786","title":"Cal33 CDX smTEADi, rep3"},{"accession":"GSM8532787","title":"Cal33 CDX Vehicle, rep1"},{"accession":"GSM8532789","title":"Cal33 CDX Vehicle, rep3"},{"accession":"GSM8532790","title":"Cal33 CDX pTEADi, rep1"},{"accession":"GSM8532784","title":"Cal33 CDX smTEADi, rep1"},{"accession":"GSM8532785","title":"Cal33 CDX smTEADi, rep2"},{"accession":"GSM8532793","title":"Cal33 CDX Control, rep1"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":12,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["39826667"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE277nnn/GSE277859/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1164651"},"200145057":{"uid":"200145057","accession":"GSE145057","gds":"","title":"Establishment of a human tongue cancer organoid biobank enables early diagnosis, prognosis, and identification of therapeutic targets","summary":"Tongue cancer (TC) is the most frequent and a serious type of oral cancer with major clinical challenges such as lymph node metastasis and the appearance of chemotherapy resistant cells. Thus, development of diagnostic and therapeutic strategies to target these malignant cancer cells is urgently required. Here, we describe a novel and highly efficient method to generate human TC organoids, thereby creating a TC organoid biobank with primary and metastatic TC from 28 patients with diverse ages and cancer stages. These organoid lines can be expanded, passed, stored frozen for long periods, and they can reproduce original TC tissues in vitro and in xenograft models. The organoids showed different properties among patients with respect to the proliferation capacity and susceptibility to cisplatin, a commonly used chemotherapeutic agent in TC therapy. This suggests that TC organoids are useful for accurate risk grading and predicting the prognosis at early stages of TC, which is difficult to diagnose clinically. Thus, human TC organoids are useful for profiling TCs, which will lead to drug development against metastatic and chemotherapy-resistant TCs.","gpl":"18573","gse":"145057","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2024/09/13","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM4305532","title":"TumorOrg.P13"},{"accession":"GSM4305529","title":"TumorOrg.P08.CDDPResistant_Rep1"},{"accession":"GSM7928137","title":"TumorOrg.P32.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305535","title":"TumorOrg.P25"},{"accession":"GSM7928138","title":"NormalOrg.P32.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305536","title":"TumorTissue.P08"},{"accession":"GSM4305533","title":"TumorOrg.P18"},{"accession":"GSM7928135","title":"TumorOrg.P21.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305524","title":"NormalOrg.P21"},{"accession":"GSM7928132","title":"TumorOrg.P32"},{"accession":"GSM4305531","title":"TumorOrg.P08"},{"accession":"GSM4305530","title":"TumorOrg.P08.CDDPResistant_Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM7928136","title":"TumorOrg.P25.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305528","title":"TumorOrg.P03"},{"accession":"GSM7928133","title":"TumorOrg.P03.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305527","title":"NormalTissue.P13"},{"accession":"GSM4305522","title":"NormalOrg.P08"},{"accession":"GSM7928130","title":"TumorOrg.P08.Rep2"},{"accession":"GSM4305525","title":"NormalOrg.P25"},{"accession":"GSM7928131","title":"TumorOrg.P15"},{"accession":"GSM4305523","title":"NormalOrg.P13"},{"accession":"GSM4305526","title":"NormalTissue.P08"},{"accession":"GSM4305537","title":"TumorTissue.P13"},{"accession":"GSM4305534","title":"TumorOrg.P21"},{"accession":"GSM7928134","title":"TumorOrg.P18.Rep2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP248010","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP248/SRP248010/"}],"n_samples":25,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE145nnn/GSE145057/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA605814"},"200270047":{"uid":"200270047","accession":"GSE270047","gds":"","title":"Analytical performance of OncoPrism-HNSCC, an RNA-based assay to inform immune checkpoint inhibitor treatment decisions for recurrent/metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","summary":"While immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) therapies can significantly improve outcomes for patients with recurrent/metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (RM-HNSCC), only about 15–20% benefit from such treatments. Clinical tests that guide the use of ICIs are therefore critically needed. OncoPrism-HNSCC was developed to address this need. The assay combines next generation RNA sequencing-based immunomodulatory gene expression signatures with machine learning algorithms to generate an OncoPrism Score that classifies patients as having low, medium, or high likelihood of disease control in response to ICI treatment. Also, OncoPrism-HNSCC leverages the same FFPE patient tumor RNA used for ICI response prediction to identify rare cases where oncogenic rearrangements in NTRK1/2/3 or ALK genes, which may indicate the use of potentially highly effective targeted therapies. The clinical performance of OncoPrism-HNSCC has been validated. Here, we report its analytical performance in the presence of potentially confounding sources of variation.","gpl":"18573","gse":"270047","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2024/09/02","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM8333535","title":"8J361, 80 ng RNA input, rep B"},{"accession":"GSM8333452","title":"THWJ7, operator 2, lot A, day 2, rep C"},{"accession":"GSM8333664","title":"RNA-08, 54.0 % DV200, incubation time 1 min, rep 18"},{"accession":"GSM8333581","title":"R69R3, 40 ng RNA input, rep A"},{"accession":"GSM8333369","title":"195NM, operator 1, lot B, day 1, rep C"},{"accession":"GSM8333701","title":"12CU1, 13.0 % DV200, incubation time 5 min, rep A"},{"accession":"GSM8333498","title":"195NM, operator 2, lot B, day 2, rep B"},{"accession":"GSM8333332","title":"OODZN, operator 1, lot B, day 2, rep C, alternate sequencer"},{"accession":"GSM8333415","title":"VCNJ7, operator 2, lot B, day 1, rep B"},{"accession":"GSM8333618","title":"LNRMW, 0 % gDNA, rep R2"},{"accession":"GSM8333306","title":"195NM, operator 2, lot A, day 1, rep A, alternate sequencer"},{"accession":"GSM8333518","title":"VA8LQ, 40 ng RNA input, rep D"},{"accession":"GSM8333555","title":"GU1HL, 10 ng RNA input, rep B"},{"accession":"GSM8333472","title":"THWJ7, operator 1, lot A, day 2, rep C"},{"accession":"GSM8333389","title":"195NM, operator 2, lot A, day 1, rep C"},{"accession":"GSM8333684","title":"RNA-11, 22.0 % DV200, incubation time 