ings show that in addition to normal tissue sparing, FLASH could overcome hypoxia-mediated tumor resistance. Follow-up molecular analysis using RNAseq profiling uncovered a FLASH-specific profile in human GBM that involved cell-cycle arrest, decreased ribosomal biogenesis, and a switch from oxidative phosphorylation to glycolysis. Glycolysis inhibition by trametinib enhanced FLASH efficacy in both normal and clamped conditions.  Conclusions: These data provide new and specific insights showing the efficacy of FLASH in a radiation-resistant context, proving an additional benefit of FLASH over CONV.","gpl":"20301","gse":"223607","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2024/01/24","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM6965391","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT hyperoxia, late, biol rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM6965437","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT physioxia, late, biol rep 3"},{"accession":"GSM6965394","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT hypoxia, late, biol rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM6965397","title":"Tumor, No-RT hypoxia, late, biol rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM6965414","title":"Tumor, No-RT hypoxia, 24 hr, biol rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM6965417","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT hypoxia, late, biol rep 4"},{"accession":"GSM6965434","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT physioxia, 24 hr, biol rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM6965400","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT hyperoxia, late, biol rep 3"},{"accession":"GSM6965446","title":"Tumor, No-RT hypoxia, late, biol rep 4"},{"accession":"GSM6965383","title":"Tumor, FLASH-RT hypoxia, 24 hr, biol rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM6965420","title":"Tumor, No-RT hyperoxia, late, biol rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM6965403","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT hypoxia, late, biol rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM6965423","title":"Tumor, FLASH-RT physioxia, late, biol rep 4"},{"accession":"GSM6965440","title":"Tumor, No-RT physioxia, late, biol rep 3"},{"accession":"GSM6965426","title":"Tumor, CONV-RT physio